;; Reviewed 2026-10-16 by the user (written by Claude, from
;; expected-vax-entiertrap-OC-7 and the guest run of 2026-10-16). Why
;; this is right:
;; - As expected-vax-entiertrap-6.err, but the traceback names the
;;   program section, POC_CODE, not ENTIERTRAP_INIT: under -OC the fault
;;   is past about a kilobyte into the initializer, and VMS's traceback
;;   names a routine only that far (a guest test, 2026-10-10: a fault
;;   907 bytes into a MACRO-32 routine is named by the routine, one 1107
;;   bytes in by its section).
%SYSTEM-F-FLTOVF_F, arithmetic fault, floating overflow at PC=xxxxxxxx, PSL=xxxxxxxx
%TRACE-F-TRACEBACK, symbolic stack dump follows
module name     routine name                     line       rel PC    abs PC

ENTIERTRAP      POC_CODE                                   xxxxxxxx  xxxxxxxx
ENTIERTRAP      ENTIERTRAP_MAIN                            xxxxxxxx  xxxxxxxx
